==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|provendre}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|provendre}}, variant of {{m|fro|provende||allowance, provision}}, from {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{m|la|praebenda||a payment, in {{etyl|ML.|en}} also an allowance of food and drink, pittance, also a prebend}}; see {{m|en|prebend}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈprɒvɪndə/|/ˈprɒvəndə/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈprɑːvəndɚ/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# [[food|Food]], especially for [[livestock]].
#* '''1663''', ''[[w:Hudibras|Hudibras]]'', by [[w:Samuel Butler (poet)|Samuel Butler]], part 1, [[s:Hudibras/Part 1/Canto 2|canto 2]]
#*: He ripp'd the womb up of his mother, / Dame [[Tellus]], 'cause he wanted [[fother]], / And '''provender''', wherewith to feed / Himself and his less cruel [[steed]].
# An [[edible]] material that provides [[sustenance]].

